<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Median of a dataset (odd number of values)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The heights (in cm) of <strong>{@n@}</strong> tomato seedlings were measured:</p>
<p style="background-color:#f9f9f9;padding:12px;border:1px solid #ddd;font-family:monospace;font-size:1.1em;">{@data_str@}</p>
<p>Find the <strong>median</strong> height. [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt_med]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h4>Worked solution</h4>
<p>First put the heights in order:</p>
<p style="font-family:monospace;">{@sorted@}</p>
<p>There are \(n={@n@}\) values (odd), so the median is the \(\frac{n+1}{2}={@pos@}\)-th value:</p>
\[ \text{Median} = {@med@}\text{ cm}. \]]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2026010500</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[n: 2*rand(2)+7;                       /* 7 or 9 */
data0: makelist(rand(20)+1, i, 1, n);
sorted: sort(data0);
med: sorted[(n+1)/2];
data: random_permutation(data0);
for tries:1 thru 20 do (if data[(n+1)/2] # med then return(), data: random_permutation(data0));
unsorted_mid: data[(n+1)/2];
pos: (n+1)/2;
mean_val: apply("+", data)/n;
data_str: sconcat(data[1]);
for i:2 thru n do data_str: sconcat(data_str, ", ", data[i]);]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
    <specificfeedback format="html">
      <text/>
    </specificfeedback>
    <questionnote format="html">
      <text>n={@n@}, median={@med@}</text>
    </questionnote>
